<statement>
<p>
Solve the following linear system.  If the system has an infinite number of solutions, parameterize the solution set in terms of the free variables of the original system.</p>
<p>
<m>\displaystyle{\left\lbrace\begin{array}{ccccccc} -{4}{x}\amp+\amp{3}{y}\amp+\amp{17}{z}\amp=\amp-{24}\\{5}{x}\amp-\amp{8}{y}\amp-\amp{17}{z}\amp=\amp{47}\\-{2}{x}\amp+\amp{4}{y}\amp+\amp{6}{z}\amp=\amp-{22}\end{array}\right.}</m></p>
<p>
x = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
y = <fillin characters="20"/>  
</p>
<p>
z = <fillin characters="20"/>  

</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li><m>\displaystyle{3}+{5}{z}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle-{4}+{1}{z}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle{z}</m></li></ul></p>
</answer>

